IMPORT prelude

-- The Schedule of the Interpretation Act 1978 (Northern Territory), "Ordinances repealed", and section 2(1) and (2) which point at it.
-- Reprint as in force at 21 April 2023.
--
-- The Schedule has four Parts.
-- Parts 1, 2 and 3 list Ordinances that section 2(1) repeals.
-- Part 4 lists two South Australian Acts that section 2(2) says cease to have effect in the Northern Territory as laws of the Northern Territory.
-- The table below has one entry for each line of the Schedule that names an instrument, with its Part and the name as printed; a script that reads the text file wrote it.
-- A function answers JUST where the text says what the Act does to an instrument, and NOTHING for an instrument the Schedule does not name.

DECLARE `Instrument named in the Schedule` HAS
    `part of the Schedule`  IS A NUMBER
    `name as printed`       IS A STRING
    `line in the text file` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `What section 2 does to an instrument` IS ONE OF
    `repeals the instrument`
    `ends the instrument's effect in the Northern Territory as a law of the Northern Territory`

-- src:927 | Interpretation Ordinance 1931
@ref Schedule, Part 1 (src:927)
`instrument at line 927` MEANS `Instrument named in the Schedule` OF 1, "Interpretation Ordinance 1931", 927

