GIVEN name IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Instrument named in the Schedule`)
`the Schedule entry printed for` MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN entry IS A `Instrument named in the Schedule` YIELD entry's `name as printed` EQUALS name) `instruments named in the Schedule`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST x

-- Section 2(1): the Ordinances set out in Parts 1, 2 and 3 of the Schedule are repealed.
-- Section 2(2): the laws of the State of South Australia set out in Part 4 of the Schedule cease to have effect in the Northern Territory as laws of the Northern Territory.
-- src:153 | (1) The Ordinances set out in Parts 1, 2 and 3 of the Schedule are repealed.
-- src:154 | (2) The laws of the State of South Australia set out in Part 4 of the Schedule cease to have effect in the Northern Territory as laws of the Northern Territory.
@ref s 2(1), (2) (src:153-154)
GIVEN name IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE (`What section 2 does to an instrument`)
`s 2(1), (2): what this Act does to the instrument named` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Schedule entry printed for` name
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST entry THEN
        IF   entry's `part of the Schedule` AT MOST 3
        THEN JUST `repeals the instrument`
        ELSE JUST `ends the instrument's effect in the Northern Territory as a law of the Northern Territory`
